20:    objects.
21:
22:    Rule
23:    Order the color groups by their leftmost occupied column, creating output
24:    columns from left to right with one background column between groups. Within
25:    each color group, order its objects by decreasing bbox left column, crop
26:    each object mask to its bbox, and stack those objects top-to-bottom in that
27:    order with one background row between them. Bottom-align each color stack on
28:    the original-size output canvas.
29:
30:    Key insight
31:    Original position is used as ordering information: color groups sort
32:    left-to-right, while objects inside a color sort right-to-left before being
33:    repacked at the bottom.
34:    """
35:    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
